message: "If you use or reference AGM, please cite it as below."
title: "AGM: An Afferent Self-Model for Interpretable, Self-Monitoring AI Agents"
authors:
  - family-names: Parnell
    given-names: Alexander
    affiliation: Vektorgeist
abstract: >-
  AGM is a self-model composed of three organs — Aitia (cause), Gut (instinct), and Metron
  (measure) — that sits beside a language-model agent and observes it. Its defining constraint
  is the Enoptron principle: AGM is afferent-only. It reports upward to the operator and sideways
  into the agent's internal mood, but never re-enters the answer, becomes memory, or gates a
  component. A self-model permitted to steer the output stops being an honest mirror and becomes
  an unobservable controller; afferent-only keeps it honest. AGM is the flagship pillar of the
  Vektorgeist Method (VGM).
keywords:
  - AI agents
  - interpretability
  - self-model
  - AI safety
  - agent observability
  - drift detection
  - afferent
  - local AI
  - Vektorgeist Method
